From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Lebedev <sergey@lebedev.mobi>
Date: Mon, 28 Jul 2026 23:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: mt7530: model EN7581 port 5 as TRGMII-capable

en7581_mac_port_get_caps() leaves port 5 with an empty
supported_interfaces, so any DTS declaring a port@5 user port fails
phylink creation with -EINVAL ("phylink: error: empty
supported_interfaces" / "error -22 setting up PHY").

On the ZTE H267A board, the SoC's own MCM switch uplinks to the
external MT7530BU (the chip the jacks are physically wired to) over
TRGMII on port 5 -- measured live 2026-07-28 (frames from the EXT chip
count at MCM P5's RX MIB). Declare it TRGMII-capable, 1G-only (the
link runs fixed-link 1000/full). Harmless for the other EN7581 boards,
which declare no port@5 node.

Signed-off-by: Sergey Lebedev <sergey@lebedev.mobi>
---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/mt7530.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/mt7530.c
@@ -2819,6 +2819,18 @@
 		config->mac_capabilities |= MAC_10 | MAC_100 | MAC_1000FD;
 		break;
 
+	/* Port 5: board-level TRGMII uplink to the external switch (the
+	 * ZTE H267A wires its jacks to a second MT7530BU behind this
+	 * port). Unused on the other EN7581 boards, which declare no
+	 * port@5 node.
+	 */
+	case 5:
+		__set_bit(PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_TRGMII,
+			  config->supported_interfaces);
+
+		config->mac_capabilities |= MAC_1000FD;
+		break;
+
 	/* Port 6 is connected to SoC's XGMII MAC. There is no MII pinout. */
 	case 6:
 		__set_bit(PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_INTERNAL,
